#@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
#@type = "provisioning.security"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning Worker Admin Permissions
	Testing to assure that provisioning account worker admin permissions works properly.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a provisioning user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | provisioning.admin                    |
	| Email Address | provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Provisioning                          |
	| Last Name     | Admin                                 |
	* I assign the provisioning user with the email address "provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken" to the provisioning role "Provisioning Admin"
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | prm.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRM                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | prm.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRM                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | prm.koroneiki3                       |
	| Email Address | prm.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRM                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki3                           |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Misper - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| Permission Partner |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Misper - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| MISPERPERMIS |
	| MISPER       |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| MISPERPERMIS |
	| MISPER       |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Liferay Permissioning Role |
	| Second Permissioning Role  |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Misper - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| prm.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Permis - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Misper - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from provisioning
	| provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken |

Scenario: Assign worker
	Testing the ability to create a worker in Dossiera and koroneiki and assigning the worker to an account via provisioning

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Misper - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRM                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | prm.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRM                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki3                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Permis - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I create a team with the name "Permission Partner" for the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I assign the team with the name "Permission Partner" on the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "Permission Partner"
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address          | prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name             | PRM                                  |
	| Language               | English                              |
	| Last Name              | Koroneiki2                           |
	| Email Address Verified | true                                 |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the Liferay worker role for accounts |
	| Name        | Liferay Permissioning Role                   |
	| Type        | Account Worker                               |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticProvisioningQaUserPassword}"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Permis"
	And I click on the account with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Liferay Workers" tab
	And I click on the assign worker button
	And I populate and save the assign worker form with the following values
	| Email Address | prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Assign Role   | Liferay Permissioning Role             |
	Then I should be able to view the worker with the email address "prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | PRM Koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Role          | Liferay Permissioning Role           |
	| User Status   | VERIFIED                             |
	And I should not be able to view the worker with the email address "prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And the account with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" should be assigned the contact with the email address "prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the customer contact role "Support User"
	And the account with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" should be assigned the contact with the email address "prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" with the worker contact role "Liferay Permissioning Role"
	When I click on the "Contacts" tab
	Then I should be able to view the contact with the email address "prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | PRM Koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Role          | Support User                         |
	| User Status   | VERIFIED                             |
	And I should not be able to view the contact with the email address "prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I click on the "History" tab
	Then the history entry with the keywords "Auto > Assigned Contact" and "PRM Koroneiki1" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Assigned Contact > PRM Koroneiki1 |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                             |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                      |
	| Update Field New Value      | Support User                             |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Provisioning Admin > Assigned Contact" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Provisioning Admin > Assigned Contact > PRM Koroneiki2 |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                                           |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                    |
	| Update Field New Value      | Liferay Permissioning Role                             |

Scenario: Unassign worker
	Testing the ability to create a workers in Dossiera and unassigning the worker to an account via provisioning

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Misper - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRM                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | prm.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRM                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki3                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Permis - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I create a team with the name "Permission Partner" for the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I assign the team with the name "Permission Partner" on the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "Permission Partner"
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address          | prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name             | PRM                                  |
	| Language               | English                              |
	| Last Name              | Koroneiki2                           |
	| Email Address Verified | true                                 |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the Liferay worker role for accounts |
	| Name        | Liferay Permissioning Role                   |
	| Type        | Account Worker                               |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Liferay Permissioning Role |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "provisioning.admin@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticProvisioningQaUserPassword}"
	And I update my password upon login to "test"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Permis"
	And I click on the account with the name "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Liferay Workers" tab
	And I click on the "Unassign" button in the dropdown menu for the worker with the email address "prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	Then I should not be able to view the worker with the email address "prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And I should not be able to view the worker with the email address "prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And the contact with the email address "prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be assigned the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}"
	When I click on the "Contacts" tab
	Then I should be able to view the contact with the email address "prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | PRM Koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Role          | Support User                         |
	| User Status   | VERIFIED                             |
	And I should not be able to view the contact with the email address "prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I click on the "History" tab
	Then the history entry with the keywords "Auto > Assigned Contact" and "PRM Koroneiki1" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Assigned Contact > PRM Koroneiki1 |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                             |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                      |
	| Update Field New Value      | Support User                             |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Koroneiki QA Service Producer > Assigned Contact" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Koroneiki QA Service Producer > Assigned Contact > PRM Koroneiki2 |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                                                      |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                               |
	| Update Field New Value      | Liferay Permissioning Role                                        |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Provisioning Admin > Unassigned Contact" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Provisioning Admin > Unassigned Contact > PRM Koroneiki2 |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                                             |
	| Update Field Original Value | Liferay Permissioning Role                               |
	| Update Field New Value      | N/A                                                      |

Scenario: Update worker role
	Testing the ability to create a worker in koroneiki and updating the respective contact roles in the provisioning account details page

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Misper - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRM                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | prm.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRM                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki3                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Permis - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I create a team with the name "Permission Partner" for the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I assign the team with the name "Permission Partner" on the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "Permission Partner"
	| prm.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address          | prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name             | PRM                                  |
	| Language               | English                              |
	| Last Name              | Koroneiki2                           |
	| Email Address Verified | true                                 |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the Liferay worker role for accounts |
	| Name        | Liferay Permissioning Role                   |
	| Type        | Account Worker                               |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the second worker role for accounts |
	| Name        | Second Permissioning Role                   |
	| Type        | Account Worker                              |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "prm.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Permis - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
